---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Tile from '../components/Tile.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
---
<Base title="About" description="Who I am and why this site exists.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="label">About</p>
      <div><h1>I’m KV, and I like making things</h1></div>
    </header>
    <div class="body">
      <div class="portrait">
        <!-- Swap this tile for a real photo: <img src="/kv.jpg" alt="KV" class="photo" /> -->
        <Tile seed="kv-portrait" palette="dune" w={420} ratio={0.82} inline>
          <div class="glass solid">
            <div class="g-head"><span>KV</span><span class="g-dim">Builder</span></div>
            <div class="g-row"><span class="g-dim">Day job</span><span>Software</span></div>
            <div class="g-row"><span class="g-dim">Side</span><span>Products</span></div>
            <div class="g-row"><span class="g-dim">Based</span><span>Earth</span></div>
          </div>
        </Tile>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p><strong>Replace this with your story.</strong> A good about page answers three questions: who are you, what do you make, and why should a stranger care?</p>
        <p>Here’s a starting draft. I’m a builder. I spend my days writing software and my evenings and weekends building side products — some useful, some silly, a few that actually make money. Mind of KV is my public notebook: where I document what I’m building, what I’m learning, and the ideas I can’t stop thinking about.</p>
        <h2>Why “Mind of KV”?</h2>
        <p>Because it’s deliberately broad. I don’t want to be the “X person.” I want this to be wherever curiosity goes next, held together by one thread: I build things.</p>
        <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/articles">Writing</a> — essays on building, thinking clearly and doing good work.</li>
          <li><a href="/videos">Videos</a> — build logs, walkthroughs and conversations.</li>
          <li><a href="/series">Series</a> — multi-part deep dives on a single theme.</li>
          <li><a href="/building">Products</a> — everything I’m building, with the numbers.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Say hello</h2>
        <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, reply to any newsletter, or find me on {SITE.socials.map((s, i) => <>{i > 0 && (i === SITE.socials.length - 1 ? ' or ' : ', ')}<a href={s.href}>{s.label}</a></>)}.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div style="height:128px"></div>
</Base>
<style>
  .body { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 24px; }
  .portrait { grid-column: 1 / 3; position: sticky; top: 100px; align-self: start; padding-right: 48px; }
  .prose { grid-column: 3 / 5; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 64px; } .portrait, .prose { grid-column: 1; position: static; padding: 0; } }
</style>
